  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{f}^{2}-2af+{a}^{2}=(f-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n-24f+144+{f}^{2}={f}^{2}-24f+144\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{2}-24f+{12}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{2}-2\\cdot 12f+{12}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=12.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f-12)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
